1. Central Processing Unit (CPU) - category is processor , brain of the computer and processes every program , click and instructions, its position is on the CPU
socket of motherboard (its a small chip)

2. Hard Disk Drive (HDD) - category is Storage, stores files permanently keeps everything stored even there is no power provided and it uses magnetic disks with 
other moving parts , placed inside drive bay (A dedicated physical slot or compartment designed to securely mount and hold internal storage devices)

3. Solid State Drive (SSD) - category is Storage, stores files , apps and operting system , works same as HDD only difference is its a bit faster than HDD and its
silent and has no moving parts , placed in M.2 slot on motherboard

4. Laptop power charger - category is power supply, it basically converts AC power from the wall into DC as required by the computer

5. Input/Output Panel (I/O) - category is input output, contains all the ports from outside the machine , everything we plug into machine goes through this 
position is at the rear of I/O slot at the edge of chassis (outer frame of cpu the metal box) 

6. Desktop graphics processing unit (GPU) - category visual input, creates everything we see on screen handles images videos and all the stuff basically
position is at the PCle x16 slot on the motherboard

7. Network adapter - catergory is connectivity , it gives the ability of connecting the computer to internet without it the machine cannot go online
position is at PCle x1 slot on the motherboard

8. USB Wifi dongle - category is connectivity, gives wireless access to computers and connects the machine to internet 

9. Power supply unit (PSU) - category is power, takes electricity from power socket and converts it into right voltage for each component position is at the edge of 
chasis 

10. Random Access Memory (RAM) - category is memory , it temporary stores on what the computer is working on , makes data fast to access , everything is lost when
power is not provided, position is on DIMM slots on motherboard  

